Regions - collection of DC’s interconnected by a low latency NW.  
Availability zones - DC's , physically separate locations with in each region. Not every region supports AZ
Availability zone services 
1) Zonal - we can select the AZ’s in which we want to deploy the service
        Then duplicate service is deployed in another AZ. 
2) Zone redundant - Azure select the AZ’s for us automatically  , will deploy in more than one AZ
3) Always available service - global services, non regional services.  Eg: Entra ID, Azure portal.

Resources - Azure services that we have access to 
Resource groups - logical grouping of resources. Grouping should be based of lifecycle etc
	A resource must belong to only 1 resource group
Subscriptions - billing unit. 
        Every resource must exist inside 1 subscription.
	A user can have more than 1 subscription. 
        User who is not part of a subscription cant see the resources inside it.
        When organization &  subscriptions scales then to avoid complexity of increased subscription management groups is used
Management group - We have root management group and sub management group and sub management group may be connected to a subscription . 
                Every subscription can be connected to only 1 management group but a management group can have multiple subscriptions
                Root management group + max 5 management groups only can be the size = max 6 
                 (use : inheritance , apply policy/rule at root level so that it will get applied to all) 

